{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Peter Visits Vanessa in San Francisco", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Calling the Boss", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 6, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 4, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "A2.2", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Describe characteristics of different people and their jobs in common social situations.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. ", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. ", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. ", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you hear at work.", "type": "text"}]}, {"content": "engenn5le04ob06re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Simple Present vs. Present Continuous Tenses", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You use the Simple Present tense to talk about:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<ul> <li>a routine action or specific action that happens regularly</li> <li>a general truth</li> <li>to give personal information</li> </ul> ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You can use expressions of frequency like <span class=\"italic\">every day</span> or <span class=\"italic\">always</span> with the Present Simple.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You form the Present Continuous with the verb <span class=\"strong\">to be + verb-ing</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You use the Present Continuous tense to talk about:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<ul> <li>a current event or action happening around now</li> <li>events that <span class=\"strong\">are going to happen</span> soon (future plans)</li> </ul> ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You can use expressions like <span class=\"italic\">right now</span> or <span class=\"italic\">later</span> with the Present Continuous.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Present Tense\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Present Continuous Tense\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I have three weeks of vacation left.</br></br>  Your benefit plan allows you to take 3 personal days during the year.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I am calling to ask for a few days off in the next few days.</br></br>   I am hoping I can use some vacation time next week.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Asking for Clarification", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "If you don't understand what a person is saying, it is important to ask for clarification in a polite way.   </br></br>Here are some expressions you can use to ask for clarification.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<ul> <li>Could you clarify what you mean by that?</li> <li>What do you mean by ... ?</li> <li>Do you mean ... ?</li> <li>Could you be more explicit about that?</li> <li>Could you give me an example?</li> </ul>", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to earn", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to obtain after doing something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You must earn those days off. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le04ob06aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "holiday", "type": "name"}, {"content": "vacation; time you do not work", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You will have 3 weeks for a holiday at the end of your first year.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le04ob06aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "benefit plan", "type": "name"}, {"content": "extra advantages connected to a job, like health insurance", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Your benefit plan includes personal days and health insurance.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le04ob06aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "personal day", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a day you do not work, you do other things (but not vacation)", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You can take three personal days during the year. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le04ob06aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "head chef", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the person who is responsible for the kitchen in a restaurant", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You can use those days if your head chef agrees.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le04ob06aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "manager", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a person who organizes the work of other people", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I'm just a good manager.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le04ob06aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "boss", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the person who is in charge of a workplace", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Thank you Mr. Johnson! You're a great boss!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le04ob06aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Write a dialogue of 7 to 9 lines. One person is the worker. The other person is the boss or manager.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Ask for time off.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Use expressions asking for clarification.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Practice your dialogue with a partner.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Change roles.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I write 9 lines about a boss and a worker.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I ask for clarification in a dialogue.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I practice speaking with a partner.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I change roles in a dialogue.", "type": "text